# libvms_shr.vec — CANONICAL, FROZEN symbol-vector manifest for LIBVMS$SHR.EXE
# (the src/libvms VMS system services + RTL). SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for the
# universal ORDER. bead vms-bd1 (operator-approved freeze 2026-08-13), pillar
# vms-ade.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. LIBVMS$SHR's universals are DISCOVERED from `nm` of the
# compiled objects (hundreds of sys$*/lib$*/str$*/mth$*/ots$*/... names), and
# before this file the vector was emitted name-SORTED. Name-sort is deterministic
# for a fixed object set, but it is NOT append-only: adding one universal whose
# name sorts into the middle SHIFTS the index of every later universal, which
# breaks GSMATCH LEQUAL for any consumer (vmsrms, DCL) that has bound an index.
# This manifest freezes the ORDER so that established indices never move.
#
# HOW mk_libvms_shr.sh USES IT (frozen-order-then-append):
#   1. every universal listed here is emitted FIRST, in THIS order (its line
#      number is its symbol-vector index);
#   2. any universal `nm` discovers that is NOT yet listed here is APPENDED,
#      sorted, AFTER the frozen block — it never displaces a frozen index;
#   3. if a listed universal is no longer defined by the objects, the link FAILS
#      LOUDLY (retire it in place instead — set its class to PRIVATE_PROCEDURE/
#      PRIVATE_DATA and keep the line, so nothing below it moves).
# To LOCK a freshly-appended universal's index, append its `NAME=CLASS` line to
# the END of this file (and to libvms_shr.vec.frozen). Until then it rides in the
# deterministic auto-appended tail.
#
# THE INVARIANT — APPEND-ONLY. Never reorder, never delete an existing line;
# only append at the end, or retire in place. This is the OpenVMS upward-
# compatibility contract for a GSMATCH LEQUAL shareable image
# (docs/design-link-native-toolchain.md §5, from the public VSI OpenVMS Linker
# Utility Manual — clean-room, CLAUDE.md Rule 8).
#
# ENFORCEMENT. tests/integration/test_symvec_freeze.sh checks libvms_shr.vec.frozen
# is still an exact ordered prefix of this file and that no name repeats; the
# native-link graph (run_libvms_native.sh / link_native_graph) proves the BUILT
# .vms$sv reproduces this order. Reorder or drop -> RED; append -> GREEN.
#
# FORMAT: one `NAME=CLASS` per line (CLASS = PROCEDURE|DATA|PRIVATE_PROCEDURE|
# PRIVATE_DATA). `#` comments and blank lines are ignored.
